>>PROBLEM 2: IDENTIFICATION OF INDIVIDUALS
>>
>>Individuals possess rights.  But, post-singularity, drawing the lines
>>around individuals may be hard.  When intelligences join together
>>in networks, and those networks into larger networks, is each level
>>an individual, and does it have the right to suppress its constituent
>>individuals? 

Have we a right to suppress our partial personalities or memes? I would 
say that we should encourage their development as long as they enrich the 
whole system, but not if they limit or damage it.

>>Can it allow its constituent individuals to violate each
>>others' rights, as we may suppress parts of our personality?

Good question. I would probably say that higher level entities would have 
a say in what is allowed for their constituents, simply because it would 
be in their self-interest. If my partial personalities start to violate 
each other, I will not feel good. Therefore they would in this case 
violate my rights.

>>If you have five daemons in your mind, and you suppress one, is it
>>oppression?  If you join a collective personality, and it decides to
>>remake you, is it murder?  What if you have partial membership in
>>several larger individuals?  What if "you" share your memories with
>>others (possibly for a price), and "you" gain some of their memories --
>>if you go far enough in that direction, you will come to the point where
>>your mental content is not concentrated in any one information locus
>>identifiable as "you".  Etc.

Complex questions with no easy answers. 

>Good points--people with multiple personalities are dealing with
>those problems now, but the situation can only get more complicated.

I have been thinking about this a lot. I'm simply exploding with ideas
which I haven't time to explore or develop, so I have decided to try to
create several parallel copies as soon as possible after I have uploaded
myself. Not that this will solve my problem in the long run, but it will 
give me some possibility to specialize. In the end I think I would end up 
as a huge clan of interrelated and divergent entities, variously 
specialized (or non-specialized). I'm thinking of writing this as a short 
story and see what my sub-personalities would come up with (since they 
would be evolutionary forces here). 

